      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Wouldn't \"Yes\" and \"No\" mean something very similar to the Thumbs Up and Thumbs Down emojis? Also \"?\" and \"Idk\" are pretty similar in meaning too. I think having a \"?\" would be more useful and more commonly used than the \"!\" since it can mean \"I don't know\" if someone has a question, if they have a question, or if they are wondering what's wrong. I'm thinking if the devs don't want to add another emoji, then maybe replacing \"!\" with \"?\" would be preferable.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
